[{"id":0,"name":"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.filtrationObs_succ_eq_filtration","kind":"Lemma","keyword":"lemma","module":"AlphaRAR.LeanMachineLearning.IsAlgEnvSeq","package":"AlphaRAR","isProp":true,"hashes":{"meaning":"0aa410953ebc280e","local":"ba2ef78965f30fbc","content":"a2dd372071574603"},"doc":"**Trivial observations carry no information.** With `𝓞 = Unit` the σ-algebra generated by the\nfirst `n + 1` rounds together with the observation at time `n + 1` is the round filtration\n`filtration n`: the observation component of the pair is constant, so it contributes nothing.\n\nThis is what lets a conditional distribution given `(history, obs)` — the form of the upstream\n`IsAlgEnvSeq.hasCondDistrib_action` — be read as a conditional expectation given the history\nfiltration. ","statement":{"binders":[{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"Ω","role":"type","type":"Type u_1","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"𝓐","role":"type","type":"Type u_2","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":true,"name":"mΩ","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace Ω","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":true,"name":"m𝓐","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace 𝓐","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasureTheory.Measure","implicit":true,"name":"P","role":"variable","type":"MeasureTheory.Measure Ω","typeRefs":[[0,21,"MeasureTheory.Measure"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure","implicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure P","typeRefs":[[0,34,"MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure"]]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"O","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → Unit","typeRefs":[[0,1,"Nat"],[8,12,"Unit"]]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"A","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → 𝓐","typeRefs":[[0,1,"Nat"]]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"𝓨","role":"type","type":"Type u_3","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":true,"name":"m𝓨","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace 𝓨","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"Y","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → 𝓨","typeRefs":[[0,1,"Nat"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"Learning.Algorithm","implicit":true,"name":"alg","role":"variable","type":"Algorithm Unit 𝓐 𝓨","typeRefs":[[0,9,"Learning.Algorithm"],[10,14,"Unit"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"Learning.Environment","implicit":true,"name":"env","role":"variable","type":"Environment Unit 𝓐 𝓨","typeRefs":[[0,11,"Learning.Environment"],[12,16,"Unit"]]},{"explicit":true,"head":"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq","implicit":false,"name":"h","role":"hypothesis","type":"IsAlgEnvSeq O A Y alg env P","typeRefs":[[0,11,"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq"]]},{"explicit":true,"head":"Nat","implicit":false,"name":"n","role":"variable","type":"ℕ","typeRefs":[[0,1,"Nat"]]}],"conclusion":"↑h.filtrationObs (n + 1) = ↑h.filtration n","conclusionHead":"Eq","conclusionRefs":[[3,16,"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.filtrationObs"],[20,21,"HAdd.hAdd"],[25,26,"Eq"],[30,40,"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.filtration"]],"decl":"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.filtrationObs_succ_eq_filtration"},"code":"/-- **Trivial observations carry no information.** With `𝓞 = Unit` the σ-algebra generated by the\nfirst `n + 1` rounds together with the observation at time `n + 1` is the round filtration\n`filtration n`: the observation component of the pair is constant, so it contributes nothing.\n\nThis is what lets a conditional distribution given `(history, obs)` — the form of the upstream\n`IsAlgEnvSeq.hasCondDistrib_action` — be read as a conditional expectation given the history\nfiltration. -/\nlemma filtrationObs_succ_eq_filtration {𝓨 : Type*} {m𝓨 : MeasurableSpace 𝓨} {Y : ℕ → Ω → 𝓨}\n    {alg : Algorithm Unit 𝓐 𝓨} {env : Environment Unit 𝓐 𝓨}\n    (h : IsAlgEnvSeq O A Y alg env P) (n : ℕ) :\n    h.filtrationObs (n + 1) = h.filtration n","proof":":= by\n  rw [filtrationObs_eq_comap, filtration_eq_comap]\n  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_\n  · rw [← measurable_iff_comap_le]\n    exact (measurable_iff_comap_le.mpr le_rfl).prodMk (measurable_const (a := ()))\n  · rw [← measurable_iff_comap_le]\n    exact measurable_fst.comp (measurable_iff_comap_le.mpr le_rfl)","source":{"path":"AlphaRAR/LeanMachineLearning/IsAlgEnvSeq.lean","start":48,"end":64,"url":"https://github.com/RemyDegenne/alpha-rar/blob/e7164a80baea3f4f65e108de31d2d561dd35e350/AlphaRAR/LeanMachineLearning/IsAlgEnvSeq.lean#L48-L64"},"deps":[],"outside":[],"external":[["Eq","lean4","inductive"],["HAdd.hAdd","lean4","definition"],["Learning.Algorithm","LeanMachineLearning","structure"],["Learning.Environment","LeanMachineLearning","structure"],["Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq","LeanMachineLearning","structure"],["Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.filtration","LeanMachineLearning","definition"],["Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.filtrationObs","LeanMachineLearning","definition"],["MeasurableSpace","mathlib","class"],["MeasureTheory.Filtration.seq","mathlib","definition"],["MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure","mathlib","class"],["MeasureTheory.IsZeroOrProbabilityMeasure.toIsFiniteMeasure","mathlib","instance"],["MeasureTheory.Measure","mathlib","structure"],["MeasureTheory.instIsZeroOrProbabilityMeasureOfIsProbabilityMeasure","mathlib","instance"],["Nat","lean4","inductive"],["Nat.instPreorder","mathlib","instance"],["OfNat.ofNat","lean4","definition"],["PUnit.instMeasurableSpace","mathlib","instance"],["Unit","lean4","definition"],["instAddNat","lean4","instance"],["instHAdd","lean4","instance"],["instOfNatNat","lean4","instance"]],"users":[],"sorry":false,"ownSorry":false,"sorryVia":[],"axioms":[],"change":null,"reviews":[],"claim":null,"specifies":[],"specifiedBy":[],"characterizations":[],"pulled":false,"directExternal":["Eq","HAdd.hAdd","Learning.Algorithm","Learning.Environment","Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq","Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.filtration","Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.filtrationObs","MeasurableSpace","MeasureTheory.Filtration.seq","MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure","MeasureTheory.IsZeroOrProbabilityMeasure.toIsFiniteMeasure","MeasureTheory.Measure","MeasureTheory.instIsZeroOrProbabilityMeasureOfIsProbabilityMeasure","Nat","Nat.instPreorder","OfNat.ofNat","PUnit.instMeasurableSpace","Unit","instAddNat","instHAdd","instOfNatNat"],"provenance":null,"edited":{"commit":"6af52f16df6126afeafe3ee85eb43a7c9dc0c535","date":"2026-09-12"}},{"id":1,"name":"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.condExp_feedback_stationaryEnv","kind":"Lemma","keyword":"lemma","module":"AlphaRAR.LeanMachineLearning.IsAlgEnvSeq","package":"AlphaRAR","isProp":true,"hashes":{"meaning":"5c2006371c086cf9","local":"17c66f20a85de607","content":"44372b28b9ef1dac"},"doc":"**Conditional expectation of the feedback is the mean of the arm's reward kernel.**\nUnder a stationary environment with per-arm reward kernel `ν`, the conditional expectation of\nthe response `Y n` given the action-augmented filtration `filtrationAction n` is the mean\n`ν.means (A n)` of the chosen arm's reward distribution. This is the `g = id` case of\n`condExp_feedback_comp_stationaryEnv` (equivalently, the upstream `condExp_feedback` with\n`means_stationaryEnv`). ","statement":{"binders":[{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"Ω","role":"type","type":"Type u_1","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"𝓐","role":"type","type":"Type u_2","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":true,"name":"mΩ","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace Ω","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":true,"name":"m𝓐","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace 𝓐","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"ProbabilityTheory.Kernel","implicit":true,"name":"ν","role":"variable","type":"ProbabilityTheory.Kernel 𝓐 ℝ","typeRefs":[[0,24,"ProbabilityTheory.Kernel"],[27,28,"Real"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel","implicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel ν","typeRefs":[[0,32,"ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasureTheory.Measure","implicit":true,"name":"P","role":"variable","type":"MeasureTheory.Measure Ω","typeRefs":[[0,21,"MeasureTheory.Measure"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure","implicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure P","typeRefs":[[0,34,"MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure"]]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"O","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → Unit","typeRefs":[[0,1,"Nat"],[8,12,"Unit"]]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"A","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → 𝓐","typeRefs":[[0,1,"Nat"]]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"Y","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → ℝ","typeRefs":[[0,1,"Nat"],[8,9,"Real"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"Learning.Algorithm","implicit":true,"name":"alg","role":"variable","type":"Algorithm Unit 𝓐 ℝ","typeRefs":[[0,9,"Learning.Algorithm"],[10,14,"Unit"],[17,18,"Real"]]},{"explicit":true,"head":"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq","implicit":false,"name":"h","role":"hypothesis","type":"IsAlgEnvSeq O A Y alg (stationaryEnv ν) P","typeRefs":[[0,11,"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq"],[23,36,"Learning.stationaryEnv"]]},{"explicit":true,"head":"Nat","implicit":false,"name":"n","role":"variable","type":"ℕ","typeRefs":[[0,1,"Nat"]]},{"explicit":true,"head":"MeasureTheory.Integrable","implicit":false,"name":"hint","role":"hypothesis","type":"MeasureTheory.Integrable (Y n) P","typeRefs":[[0,24,"MeasureTheory.Integrable"]]}],"conclusion":"P[Y n | ↑h.filtrationAction n] =ᵐ[P] fun ω => ν.means (A n ω)","conclusionHead":"Filter.EventuallyEq","conclusionRefs":[[6,7,"MeasureTheory.condExp"],[11,27,"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.filtrationAction"],[48,53,"ProbabilityTheory.Kernel.means"]],"decl":"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.condExp_feedback_stationaryEnv"},"code":"/-- **Conditional expectation of the feedback is the mean of the arm's reward kernel.**\nUnder a stationary environment with per-arm reward kernel `ν`, the conditional expectation of\nthe response `Y n` given the action-augmented filtration `filtrationAction n` is the mean\n`ν.means (A n)` of the chosen arm's reward distribution. This is the `g = id` case of\n`condExp_feedback_comp_stationaryEnv` (equivalently, the upstream `condExp_feedback` with\n`means_stationaryEnv`). -/\nlemma condExp_feedback_stationaryEnv (h : IsAlgEnvSeq O A Y alg (stationaryEnv ν) P) (n : ℕ)\n    (hint : Integrable (Y n) P) :\n    P[Y n | h.filtrationAction n] =ᵐ[P] fun ω ↦ ν.means (A n ω)","proof":":=\n  condExp_feedback_comp_stationaryEnv h n stronglyMeasurable_id hint","source":{"path":"AlphaRAR/LeanMachineLearning/IsAlgEnvSeq.lean","start":111,"end":120,"url":"https://github.com/RemyDegenne/alpha-rar/blob/e7164a80baea3f4f65e108de31d2d561dd35e350/AlphaRAR/LeanMachineLearning/IsAlgEnvSeq.lean#L111-L120"},"deps":[5],"outside":[],"external":[["DFunLike.coe","mathlib","definition"],["Filter.EventuallyEq","mathlib","definition"],["InnerProductSpace.toNormedSpace","mathlib","instance"],["Learning.Algorithm","LeanMachineLearning","structure"],["Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq","LeanMachineLearning","structure"],["Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.filtrationAction","LeanMachineLearning","definition"],["Learning.stationaryEnv","LeanMachineLearning","definition"],["MeasurableSpace","mathlib","class"],["MeasureTheory.Filtration.seq","mathlib","definition"],["MeasureTheory.Integrable","mathlib","definition"],["MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure","mathlib","class"],["MeasureTheory.IsZeroOrProbabilityMeasure.toIsFiniteMeasure","mathlib","instance"],["MeasureTheory.Measure","mathlib","structure"],["MeasureTheory.Measure.instFunLike","mathlib","instance"],["MeasureTheory.Measure.instOuterMeasureClass","mathlib","instance"],["MeasureTheory.ae","mathlib","definition"],["MeasureTheory.condExp","mathlib","definition"],["MeasureTheory.instIsZeroOrProbabilityMeasureOfIsProbabilityMeasure","mathlib","instance"],["MeasureTheory.integral","mathlib","definition"],["Nat","lean4","inductive"],["Nat.instPreorder","mathlib","instance"],["NonUnitalSeminormedCommRing.toNonUnitalSeminormedRing","mathlib","instance"],["NonUnitalSeminormedRing.toSeminormedAddCommGroup","mathlib","instance"],["NormedAddCommGroup","mathlib","class"],["NormedAddCommGroup.toSeminormedAddCommGroup","mathlib","instance"],["NormedCommRing.toSeminormedCommRing","mathlib","instance"],["NormedSpace","mathlib","class"],["PUnit.instMeasurableSpace","mathlib","instance"],["ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel","mathlib","class"],["ProbabilityTheory.Kernel","mathlib","structure"],["ProbabilityTheory.Kernel.instFunLike","mathlib","instance"],["PseudoMetricSpace.toUniformSpace","mathlib","instance"],["RCLike.toInnerProductSpaceReal","mathlib","instance"],["Real","mathlib","structure"],["Real.instRCLike","mathlib","instance"],["Real.measurableSpace","mathlib","instance"],["Real.normedAddCommGroup","mathlib","instance"],["Real.normedCommRing","mathlib","instance"],["Real.normedField","mathlib","instance"],["Real.pseudoMetricSpace","mathlib","instance"],["SeminormedAddCommGroup.toSeminormedAddGroup","mathlib","instance"],["SeminormedAddGroup.toContinuousENorm","mathlib","instance"],["SeminormedCommRing.toNonUnitalSeminormedCommRing","mathlib","instance"],["UniformSpace.toTopologicalSpace","mathlib","instance"],["Unit","lean4","definition"],["id","lean4","definition"]],"users":[],"sorry":false,"ownSorry":false,"sorryVia":[],"axioms":[],"change":null,"reviews":[],"claim":null,"specifies":[],"specifiedBy":[],"characterizations":[],"pulled":false,"directExternal":["Filter.EventuallyEq","InnerProductSpace.toNormedSpace","Learning.Algorithm","Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq","Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.filtrationAction","Learning.stationaryEnv","MeasurableSpace","MeasureTheory.Filtration.seq","MeasureTheory.Integrable","MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure","MeasureTheory.IsZeroOrProbabilityMeasure.toIsFiniteMeasure","MeasureTheory.Measure","MeasureTheory.Measure.instFunLike","MeasureTheory.Measure.instOuterMeasureClass","MeasureTheory.ae","MeasureTheory.condExp","MeasureTheory.instIsZeroOrProbabilityMeasureOfIsProbabilityMeasure","Nat","Nat.instPreorder","NonUnitalSeminormedCommRing.toNonUnitalSeminormedRing","NonUnitalSeminormedRing.toSeminormedAddCommGroup","NormedAddCommGroup.toSeminormedAddCommGroup","NormedCommRing.toSeminormedCommRing","PUnit.instMeasurableSpace","ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel","ProbabilityTheory.Kernel","PseudoMetricSpace.toUniformSpace","RCLike.toInnerProductSpaceReal","Real","Real.instRCLike","Real.measurableSpace","Real.normedAddCommGroup","Real.normedCommRing","Real.pseudoMetricSpace","SeminormedAddCommGroup.toSeminormedAddGroup","SeminormedAddGroup.toContinuousENorm","SeminormedCommRing.toNonUnitalSeminormedCommRing","UniformSpace.toTopologicalSpace","Unit"],"provenance":null,"edited":{"commit":"6af52f16df6126afeafe3ee85eb43a7c9dc0c535","date":"2026-09-12"}},{"id":2,"name":"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.memLp_feedback","kind":"Lemma","keyword":"lemma","module":"AlphaRAR.LeanMachineLearning.IsAlgEnvSeq","package":"AlphaRAR","isProp":true,"hashes":{"meaning":"754f5ca2549ab9a1","local":"4aebf8d63ef64fcf","content":"1322bda4902f2f82"},"doc":"**The response is in `L²` as soon as every arm's reward distribution is** (the paper's\nCondition **A**). With finitely many arms the second moments `∫ x² dν a` have a finite maximum,\nand the response's conditional law given the chosen arm is `ν (A n)`; so an `L²` hypothesis on\n`Y` need not be assumed alongside `hνk`.\n\nThe conditional law of `Y n` given the action `A n` is `ν (A n)` at every time\n(`IsAlgEnvSeq.hasCondDistrib_feedback_stationaryEnv`). ","statement":{"binders":[{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"Ω","role":"type","type":"Type u_1","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"𝓐","role":"type","type":"Type u_2","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":true,"name":"mΩ","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace Ω","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":true,"name":"m𝓐","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace 𝓐","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"ProbabilityTheory.Kernel","implicit":true,"name":"ν","role":"variable","type":"ProbabilityTheory.Kernel 𝓐 ℝ","typeRefs":[[0,24,"ProbabilityTheory.Kernel"],[27,28,"Real"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel","implicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel ν","typeRefs":[[0,32,"ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasureTheory.Measure","implicit":true,"name":"P","role":"variable","type":"MeasureTheory.Measure Ω","typeRefs":[[0,21,"MeasureTheory.Measure"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure","implicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure P","typeRefs":[[0,34,"MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure"]]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"O","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → Unit","typeRefs":[[0,1,"Nat"],[8,12,"Unit"]]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"A","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → 𝓐","typeRefs":[[0,1,"Nat"]]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"Y","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → ℝ","typeRefs":[[0,1,"Nat"],[8,9,"Real"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"Learning.Algorithm","implicit":true,"name":"alg","role":"variable","type":"Algorithm Unit 𝓐 ℝ","typeRefs":[[0,9,"Learning.Algorithm"],[10,14,"Unit"],[17,18,"Real"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"Finite","implicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"Finite 𝓐","typeRefs":[[0,6,"Finite"]]},{"explicit":true,"head":"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq","implicit":false,"name":"h","role":"hypothesis","type":"IsAlgEnvSeq O A Y alg (stationaryEnv ν) P","typeRefs":[[0,11,"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq"],[23,36,"Learning.stationaryEnv"]]},{"explicit":true,"implicit":false,"name":"hνk","role":"hypothesis","type":"∀ (a : 𝓐), MeasureTheory.MemLp (fun x => x) 2 (ν a)","typeRefs":[[11,30,"MeasureTheory.MemLp"]]},{"explicit":true,"head":"Nat","implicit":false,"name":"n","role":"variable","type":"ℕ","typeRefs":[[0,1,"Nat"]]}],"conclusion":"MeasureTheory.MemLp (Y n) 2 P","conclusionHead":"MeasureTheory.MemLp","conclusionRefs":[[0,19,"MeasureTheory.MemLp"]],"decl":"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.memLp_feedback"},"code":"/-- **The response is in `L²` as soon as every arm's reward distribution is** (the paper's\nCondition **A**). With finitely many arms the second moments `∫ x² dν a` have a finite maximum,\nand the response's conditional law given the chosen arm is `ν (A n)`; so an `L²` hypothesis on\n`Y` need not be assumed alongside `hνk`.\n\nThe conditional law of `Y n` given the action `A n` is `ν (A n)` at every time\n(`IsAlgEnvSeq.hasCondDistrib_feedback_stationaryEnv`). -/\nlemma memLp_feedback [Finite 𝓐] (h : IsAlgEnvSeq O A Y alg (stationaryEnv ν) P)\n    (hνk : ∀ a, MemLp (fun x : ℝ ↦ x) 2 (ν a)) (n : ℕ) :\n    MemLp (Y n) 2 P","proof":":= by\n  classical\n  let := Fintype.ofFinite 𝓐\n  -- A uniform bound on the arms' second moments.\n  set C : ℝ≥0∞ := ∑ a : 𝓐, ∫⁻ y, ‖y‖ₑ ^ 2 ∂(ν a) with hCdef\n  have hone : ∀ a : 𝓐, ∫⁻ y, ‖y‖ₑ ^ 2 ∂(ν a) ≠ ⊤ := by\n    intro a\n    have hfin := (hνk a).integrable_sq.hasFiniteIntegral\n    rw [hasFiniteIntegral_iff_enorm] at hfin\n    refine ne_of_lt (lt_of_le_of_lt (le_of_eq ?_) hfin)\n    exact lintegral_congr fun y ↦ by rw [enorm_pow]\n  have hC : C ≠ ⊤ := by\n    rw [hCdef]\n    exact (ENNReal.sum_lt_top.mpr fun a _ ↦ (hone a).lt_top).ne\n  have hb : ∀ a : 𝓐, ∫⁻ y, ‖y‖ₑ ^ 2 ∂(ν a) ≤ C :=\n    fun a ↦ Finset.single_le_sum (f := fun a ↦ ∫⁻ y, ‖y‖ₑ ^ 2 ∂(ν a))\n      (fun _ _ ↦ zero_le) (Finset.mem_univ a)\n  have hmeas : AEStronglyMeasurable (Y n) P := (h.measurable_feedback n).aestronglyMeasurable\n  exact memLp_two_of_hasCondDistrib hC (h.hasCondDistrib_feedback_stationaryEnv n) hmeas hb","source":{"path":"AlphaRAR/LeanMachineLearning/IsAlgEnvSeq.lean","start":66,"end":93,"url":"https://github.com/RemyDegenne/alpha-rar/blob/e7164a80baea3f4f65e108de31d2d561dd35e350/AlphaRAR/LeanMachineLearning/IsAlgEnvSeq.lean#L66-L93"},"deps":[],"outside":[],"external":[["AddCommMonoidWithOne.toAddMonoidWithOne","mathlib","instance"],["AddMonoidWithOne.toNatCast","mathlib","instance"],["ContinuousENorm.toENorm","mathlib","instance"],["DFunLike.coe","mathlib","definition"],["ENNReal","mathlib","definition"],["ENNReal.instAddCommMonoidWithOne","mathlib","instance"],["Finite","mathlib","class"],["Learning.Algorithm","LeanMachineLearning","structure"],["Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq","LeanMachineLearning","structure"],["Learning.stationaryEnv","LeanMachineLearning","definition"],["MeasurableSpace","mathlib","class"],["MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure","mathlib","class"],["MeasureTheory.IsZeroOrProbabilityMeasure.toIsFiniteMeasure","mathlib","instance"],["MeasureTheory.Measure","mathlib","structure"],["MeasureTheory.MemLp","mathlib","definition"],["MeasureTheory.instIsZeroOrProbabilityMeasureOfIsProbabilityMeasure","mathlib","instance"],["Nat","lean4","inductive"],["Nat.instAtLeastTwoHAddOfNat","mathlib","instance"],["Nat.instNeZeroSucc","lean4","instance"],["NonUnitalSeminormedCommRing.toNonUnitalSeminormedRing","mathlib","instance"],["NonUnitalSeminormedRing.toSeminormedAddCommGroup","mathlib","instance"],["NormedCommRing.toSeminormedCommRing","mathlib","instance"],["OfNat.ofNat","lean4","definition"],["PUnit.instMeasurableSpace","mathlib","instance"],["ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel","mathlib","class"],["ProbabilityTheory.Kernel","mathlib","structure"],["ProbabilityTheory.Kernel.instFunLike","mathlib","instance"],["PseudoMetricSpace.toUniformSpace","mathlib","instance"],["Real","mathlib","structure"],["Real.measurableSpace","mathlib","instance"],["Real.normedCommRing","mathlib","instance"],["Real.pseudoMetricSpace","mathlib","instance"],["SeminormedAddCommGroup.toSeminormedAddGroup","mathlib","instance"],["SeminormedAddGroup.toContinuousENorm","mathlib","instance"],["SeminormedAddGroup.toPseudoMetricSpace","mathlib","instance"],["SeminormedCommRing.toNonUnitalSeminormedCommRing","mathlib","instance"],["UniformSpace.toTopologicalSpace","mathlib","instance"],["Unit","lean4","definition"],["instOfNatAtLeastTwo","mathlib","instance"],["instOfNatNat","lean4","instance"]],"users":[],"sorry":false,"ownSorry":false,"sorryVia":[],"axioms":[],"change":null,"reviews":[],"claim":null,"specifies":[],"specifiedBy":[],"characterizations":[],"pulled":false,"directExternal":["AddCommMonoidWithOne.toAddMonoidWithOne","AddMonoidWithOne.toNatCast","ContinuousENorm.toENorm","DFunLike.coe","ENNReal","ENNReal.instAddCommMonoidWithOne","Finite","Learning.Algorithm","Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq","Learning.stationaryEnv","MeasurableSpace","MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure","MeasureTheory.IsZeroOrProbabilityMeasure.toIsFiniteMeasure","MeasureTheory.Measure","MeasureTheory.MemLp","MeasureTheory.instIsZeroOrProbabilityMeasureOfIsProbabilityMeasure","Nat","Nat.instAtLeastTwoHAddOfNat","Nat.instNeZeroSucc","NonUnitalSeminormedCommRing.toNonUnitalSeminormedRing","NonUnitalSeminormedRing.toSeminormedAddCommGroup","NormedCommRing.toSeminormedCommRing","OfNat.ofNat","PUnit.instMeasurableSpace","ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel","ProbabilityTheory.Kernel","ProbabilityTheory.Kernel.instFunLike","PseudoMetricSpace.toUniformSpace","Real","Real.measurableSpace","Real.normedCommRing","Real.pseudoMetricSpace","SeminormedAddCommGroup.toSeminormedAddGroup","SeminormedAddGroup.toContinuousENorm","SeminormedAddGroup.toPseudoMetricSpace","SeminormedCommRing.toNonUnitalSeminormedCommRing","UniformSpace.toTopologicalSpace","Unit","instOfNatAtLeastTwo","instOfNatNat"],"provenance":null,"edited":{"commit":"6af52f16df6126afeafe3ee85eb43a7c9dc0c535","date":"2026-09-12"}},{"id":3,"name":"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.condExp_feedback_comp_stationaryEnv","kind":"Lemma","keyword":"lemma","module":"AlphaRAR.LeanMachineLearning.IsAlgEnvSeq","package":"AlphaRAR","isProp":true,"hashes":{"meaning":"7ca0d37c3f10b03c","local":"ad4334c36f27bc4d","content":"d5bc23abf7242bf1"},"doc":"**Conditional expectation of a function of the feedback given the history and the action.**\nUnder a stationary environment with per-arm reward kernel `ν`, the conditional\nexpectation of `g (Y n)` given the action-augmented filtration `filtrationAction n`\n(the history up to `n-1` together with the current action `A n`) is the integral of `g`\nagainst the chosen arm's reward distribution, `∫ x, g x ∂(ν (A n))`. This is the crux behind\nthe response martingale (and its quadratic variation): the fresh randomness of a step is the\nresponse, revealed *after* the arm is chosen. This is the upstream `condExp_feedback_comp`\n(whose kernel is `env.feedback n` applied to the history, the observation and the action) with the\nstationary environment's feedback kernel `ν.prodMkLeft` read off. ","statement":{"binders":[{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"Ω","role":"type","type":"Type u_1","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"𝓐","role":"type","type":"Type u_2","typeRefs":[]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":true,"name":"mΩ","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace Ω","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasurableSpace","implicit":true,"name":"m𝓐","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace 𝓐","typeRefs":[[0,15,"MeasurableSpace"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"ProbabilityTheory.Kernel","implicit":true,"name":"ν","role":"variable","type":"ProbabilityTheory.Kernel 𝓐 ℝ","typeRefs":[[0,24,"ProbabilityTheory.Kernel"],[27,28,"Real"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel","implicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel ν","typeRefs":[[0,32,"ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasureTheory.Measure","implicit":true,"name":"P","role":"variable","type":"MeasureTheory.Measure Ω","typeRefs":[[0,21,"MeasureTheory.Measure"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure","implicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure P","typeRefs":[[0,34,"MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure"]]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"O","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → Unit","typeRefs":[[0,1,"Nat"],[8,12,"Unit"]]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"A","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → 𝓐","typeRefs":[[0,1,"Nat"]]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"Y","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → ℝ","typeRefs":[[0,1,"Nat"],[8,9,"Real"]]},{"explicit":false,"head":"Learning.Algorithm","implicit":true,"name":"alg","role":"variable","type":"Algorithm Unit 𝓐 ℝ","typeRefs":[[0,9,"Learning.Algorithm"],[10,14,"Unit"],[17,18,"Real"]]},{"explicit":true,"head":"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq","implicit":false,"name":"h","role":"hypothesis","type":"IsAlgEnvSeq O A Y alg (stationaryEnv ν) P","typeRefs":[[0,11,"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq"],[23,36,"Learning.stationaryEnv"]]},{"explicit":true,"head":"Nat","implicit":false,"name":"n","role":"variable","type":"ℕ","typeRefs":[[0,1,"Nat"]]},{"explicit":false,"implicit":true,"name":"g","role":"variable","type":"ℝ → ℝ","typeRefs":[[0,1,"Real"],[4,5,"Real"]]},{"explicit":true,"head":"MeasureTheory.StronglyMeasurable","implicit":false,"name":"hg","role":"hypothesis","type":"MeasureTheory.StronglyMeasurable g","typeRefs":[[0,32,"MeasureTheory.StronglyMeasurable"]]},{"explicit":true,"head":"MeasureTheory.Integrable","implicit":false,"name":"hint","role":"hypothesis","type":"MeasureTheory.Integrable (fun ω => g (Y n ω)) P","typeRefs":[[0,24,"MeasureTheory.Integrable"]]}],"conclusion":"P[fun ω => g (Y n ω) | ↑h.filtrationAction n] =ᵐ[P] fun ω => ∫ (x : ℝ), g x ∂ν (A n ω)","conclusionHead":"Filter.EventuallyEq","conclusionRefs":[[21,22,"MeasureTheory.condExp"],[26,42,"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.filtrationAction"],[61,62,"MeasureTheory.integral"],[68,69,"Real"],[76,77,"MeasureTheory.integral"]],"decl":"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.condExp_feedback_comp_stationaryEnv"},"code":"/-- **Conditional expectation of a function of the feedback given the history and the action.**\nUnder a stationary environment with per-arm reward kernel `ν`, the conditional\nexpectation of `g (Y n)` given the action-augmented filtration `filtrationAction n`\n(the history up to `n-1` together with the current action `A n`) is the integral of `g`\nagainst the chosen arm's reward distribution, `∫ x, g x ∂(ν (A n))`. This is the crux behind\nthe response martingale (and its quadratic variation): the fresh randomness of a step is the\nresponse, revealed *after* the arm is chosen. This is the upstream `condExp_feedback_comp`\n(whose kernel is `env.feedback n` applied to the history, the observation and the action) with the\nstationary environment's feedback kernel `ν.prodMkLeft` read off. -/\nlemma condExp_feedback_comp_stationaryEnv (h : IsAlgEnvSeq O A Y alg (stationaryEnv ν) P) (n : ℕ)\n    {g : ℝ → ℝ} (hg : StronglyMeasurable g) (hint : Integrable (fun ω ↦ g (Y n ω)) P) :\n    P[fun ω ↦ g (Y n ω) | h.filtrationAction n] =ᵐ[P] fun ω ↦ (ν (A n ω))[g]","proof":":= by\n  refine (h.condExp_feedback_comp n hg hint).trans ?_\n  filter_upwards with ω\n  rw [feedback_stationaryEnv, Kernel.prodMkLeft_apply]","source":{"path":"AlphaRAR/LeanMachineLearning/IsAlgEnvSeq.lean","start":95,"end":109,"url":"https://github.com/RemyDegenne/alpha-rar/blob/e7164a80baea3f4f65e108de31d2d561dd35e350/AlphaRAR/LeanMachineLearning/IsAlgEnvSeq.lean#L95-L109"},"deps":[],"outside":[],"external":[["DFunLike.coe","mathlib","definition"],["Filter.EventuallyEq","mathlib","definition"],["InnerProductSpace.toNormedSpace","mathlib","instance"],["Learning.Algorithm","LeanMachineLearning","structure"],["Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq","LeanMachineLearning","structure"],["Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq.filtrationAction","LeanMachineLearning","definition"],["Learning.stationaryEnv","LeanMachineLearning","definition"],["MeasurableSpace","mathlib","class"],["MeasureTheory.Filtration.seq","mathlib","definition"],["MeasureTheory.Integrable","mathlib","definition"],["MeasureThe